      "scenario": "description-and-meaning",
      "message": "Whats cold",
      "answer": "A cold is typically characterized by a runny nose, sneezing, sore throat, cough, and generally feeling under the weather. It often comes with a mild fever and can cause fatigue and difficulty concentrating. The duration of a typical cold ranges from 7 to 10 days. Colds are caused by viruses and are highly contagious. They spread through droplets produced when someone with a cold coughs, sneezes, or talks. There isn’t a cure for the virus itself, but treatments can help alleviate symptoms. Common remedies include using saline nasal sprays, drinking plenty of fluids, getting rest, and taking over-the-counter medications like decongestants and pain relievers.",
