    {
      "scenario": "description-and-meaning",
      "message": "I mean feeling cold, not catching a cold.",
      "answer": "Feeling cold means you’re experiencing chills or shivering because your body is losing heat faster than it’s producing it. This could be due to several factors:\n\n1. **Exposure to Cold**: Being outside in cold temperatures or being near very cold surfaces.\n2. **Illness**: Some illnesses can make you feel colder than usual, especially if you have a fever or are recovering from an infection.\n3. **Medications**: Certain medications, particularly those used to treat anxiety or depression, can make you feel colder.\n4. **Dehydration**: Not drinking enough water can lead to dehydration, making you feel colder.\n5. **Nutritional Deficiencies**: Lack of certain nutrients in your diet can affect your body’s ability to regulate temperature effectively.\n\nIf you find yourself consistently feeling cold despite wearing layers of clothing, it might be worth checking if you have any underlying health issues or nutritional deficiencies.",
